From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "D.R.racer" <drracer@seznam.cz>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 21:08:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm/sun4i: hdmi: audio: do not depend on A20 register reset
 values

The A10 HDMI controller leaves non-zero values in the audio registers
after reset (0x33 in the low byte of AUDIO_CTRL, AUDIO_FMT, STAT0, ...);
the A20 resets them to 0. On the A10:
- startup waits for AUDIO_CTRL to read 0 after the self-clearing reset,
  which never happens, so every stream open fails after 50 ms with
  "Failed to reset HDMI Audio" (-ETIMEDOUT);
- hw_params read-modify-writes AUDIO_FMT and the channel status, which
  would keep the stray bits (in the channel status: "professional",
  "non-PCM data").

Wait for the reset bit only, and write the format and the channel status
in full. On the A20 the written values are unchanged.

Tested on a Rikomagic MK802 (A10, 1 GiB).

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_hdmi_audio.c | 23 +++++++++--------------
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_hdmi_audio.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_hdmi_audio.c
index a66b6c519..48db06de8 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_hdmi_audio.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_hdmi_audio.c
@@ -82,7 +82,8 @@ static int sun4i_hdmi_audio_startup(struct snd_pcm_substream *substream,
 		     SUN4I_HDMI_AUDIO_CTRL_RESET);
 	ret = regmap_read_poll_timeout(hdmi->regmap,
 				       SUN4I_HDMI_AUDIO_CTRL_REG,
-				       reg, !reg, 100, 50000);
+				       reg, !(reg & SUN4I_HDMI_AUDIO_CTRL_RESET),
+				       100, 50000);
 	if (ret < 0) {
 		DRM_ERROR("Failed to reset HDMI Audio\n");
 		return ret;
@@ -198,10 +199,9 @@ static int sun4i_hdmi_audio_set_hw_rate(struct sun4i_hdmi *hdmi,
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
 
-	regmap_update_bits(hdmi->regmap,
-			   SUN4I_HDMI_AUDIO_STAT0_REG,
-			   SUN4I_HDMI_AUDIO_STAT0_FREQ_MASK,
-			   SUN4I_HDMI_AUDIO_STAT0_FREQ(val));
+	/* Write the whole channel status: the A10 does not reset it to 0 */
+	regmap_write(hdmi->regmap, SUN4I_HDMI_AUDIO_STAT0_REG,
+		     SUN4I_HDMI_AUDIO_STAT0_FREQ(val));
 
 	return 0;
 }
@@ -216,15 +216,10 @@ static int sun4i_hdmi_audio_set_hw_channels(struct sun4i_hdmi *hdmi,
 
 	hdmi->audio.channels = channels;
 
-	regmap_update_bits(hdmi->regmap,
-			   SUN4I_HDMI_AUDIO_FMT_REG,
-			   SUN4I_HDMI_AUDIO_FMT_LAYOUT,
-			   (channels > 2) ? SUN4I_HDMI_AUDIO_FMT_LAYOUT : 0);
-
-	regmap_update_bits(hdmi->regmap,
-			   SUN4I_HDMI_AUDIO_FMT_REG,
-			   SUN4I_HDMI_AUDIO_FMT_CH_CFG_MASK,
-			   SUN4I_HDMI_AUDIO_FMT_CH_CFG(channels));
+	/* Write the whole format: the A10 does not reset it to 0 */
+	regmap_write(hdmi->regmap, SUN4I_HDMI_AUDIO_FMT_REG,
+		     ((channels > 2) ? SUN4I_HDMI_AUDIO_FMT_LAYOUT : 0) |
+		     SUN4I_HDMI_AUDIO_FMT_CH_CFG(channels));
 
 	regmap_write(hdmi->regmap, SUN4I_HDMI_AUDIO_PCM_REG, 0x76543210);
 
-- 
